# tests/clojure-suite/MANIFEST-LIBS.sha256
#
# SHA-256 manifest of every vendored file under
# tests/clojure-suite/vendor-libs/. Same anti-cheating device as
# MANIFEST.sha256 (tests/clojure-suite/vendor/) and the same no-edit
# rule, applied to a different kind of vendored input: these are
# TEST-SUPPORT LIBRARIES (test.check, test.generative, data.generators,
# clojure.walk, clojure.template), not test files themselves. They are
# never run as suite files and never enter the scoreboard or the North
# Star denominator (see tools/clojure-suite-run.bb's `vendored` list,
# which reads tests/clojure-suite/vendor/ only) -- they exist purely so
# `require` of these namespaces resolves inside vendored test files that
# want them (numbers.clj, data_structures.clj, sequences.clj,
# transducers.clj, clojure_walk.clj, and others). `tools/verify-vendor.sh`
# re-hashes every file listed below (in addition to MANIFEST.sha256's
# vendor/ check) and fails (non-zero exit) on any mismatch, missing file,
# or extra un-manifested file in vendor-libs/.
#
# Upstream sources (byte-identical, unzipped from local ~/.m2 jars or
# copied from the pinned Clojure source checkout -- never hand-edited):
#
#   org.clojure/test.check 1.1.3 (~/.m2/repository/org/clojure/test.check/1.1.3/test.check-1.1.3.jar)
#     clojure/test/check.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/generators.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/properties.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/rose_tree.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/results.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/impl.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/clojure_test.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/clojure_test/assertions.cljc
#     clojure/test/check/random.clj   (pure-Clojure splitmix64, NOT .cljc)
#   SKIPPED from this jar (cljs-targeted, no :clj branch needs them):
#     clojure/test/check/random.cljs
#     clojure/test/check/random/doubles.cljs
#     clojure/test/check/random/longs.cljs
#     clojure/test/check/random/longs/bit_count_impl.cljs
#     clojure/test/check/clojure_test/assertions/cljs.cljc
#       -- verified by reading assertions.cljc: its own
#       `(:require-macros [...assertions.cljs])` sits inside a
#       `#?(:cljs (:require-macros ...))` reader-conditional branch, never
#       required under :clj, so vendoring the cljs sibling would be dead
#       weight.
#
#   org.clojure/test.generative 1.1.1 (~/.m2/repository/org/clojure/test.generative/1.1.1/test.generative-1.1.1.jar)
#     clojure/test/generative.clj
#   SKIPPED from this jar: clojure/test/generative/runner.clj -- pulls in
#     org.clojure/tools.namespace and uses `locking`; no vendored suite
#     file needs the runner itself, only the generative-testing macros in
#     generative.clj.
#
#   org.clojure/data.generators 1.1.0 (~/.m2/repository/org/clojure/data.generators/1.1.0/data.generators-1.1.0.jar)
#     clojure/data/generators.clj
#
#   Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6 core source, straight from .oracle/clojure-src
#     (pure Clojure, no test.* dependency of their own):
#     clojure/walk.clj
#     clojure/template.clj
#     clojure/zip.clj   (zero imports, zero host interop -- verified by
#       inspection; vendor/clojure_zip.clj is blocked solely on
#       `(:require [clojure.zip :as zip])`. clojure/xml.clj is
#       deliberately NOT vendored here -- it imports org.xml.sax classes,
#       a real JVM/SAX dependency, and stays a NOT-PORTABLE question for
#       the owner rather than a same-pattern pure-Clojure copy.)
#
#   Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6 core source, D5 -- clojure.pprint, the whole
#     eight-file library, byte-identical from .oracle/clojure-src:
#     clojure/pprint.clj              (the `ns` form + seven `load` calls)
#     clojure/pprint/utilities.clj
#     clojure/pprint/column_writer.clj
#     clojure/pprint/pretty_writer.clj
#     clojure/pprint/pprint_base.clj
#     clojure/pprint/cl_format.clj
#     clojure/pprint/dispatch.clj
#     clojure/pprint/print_table.clj
#     Unlike every other entry above, the seven files under pprint/ carry
#     NO `(ns ...)` form of their own -- each opens `(in-ns
#     'clojure.pprint)` and is pulled in by `pprint.clj`'s `(load
#     "pprint/<part>")`. The runner materializes those at their own
#     vendor-libs-relative PATH rather than at an ns-derived one; see
#     `materialize-vendor-lib-file` in tools/clojure-suite-run.bb for why
#     that is the general rule for a multi-file namespace and not a
#     pprint special case.
#     Required by vendor/printer.clj (`(:require [clojure.pprint :refer
#     [pprint]])`) and named in vendor/metadata.clj's `public-namespaces`.
#
# Counts: 22 files vendored total (9 test.check + 1 test.generative + 1
# data.generators + 3 core-source companions + 8 clojure.pprint).
#
# Regenerate (do NOT hand-edit) with:
#   cd tests/clojure-suite/vendor-libs && find . -type f | sed 's|^\./||' | sort | xargs shasum -a 256 >> MANIFEST-LIBS.sha256
# (after re-copying files byte-identically from the pinned sources above
# and re-writing this header).
#
# Format below: standard `shasum -a 256 -c` checksum lines, one per
# vendored file (paths relative to vendor-libs/), sorted by path. Lines
# starting with '#' are comments and ignored by `shasum -c`.
